This retired port packages only v0.1.9. For supported stable downloads, use the
latest stable release: https://github.com/lance-format/lance-c/releases/latest

The package lance-c provides CMake targets:

    find_package(LanceC CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_compile_features(main PRIVATE cxx_std_17)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE LanceC::lance_c)

The v0.1.9 package requires C++17 for lance.hpp; packages built from the 0.2
source line require C++20 and should request cxx_std_20 instead. The v0.1.9
package config does not propagate the language standard. C consumers include
lance/lance.h.

The default linkage matches the vcpkg triplet:
    x64-linux         → static  (LanceC::lance_c → LanceC::lance_c_static)
    x64-linux-dynamic → shared  (LanceC::lance_c → LanceC::lance_c_shared)

Override per-build by setting LanceC_LINK=static|shared before find_package.

For the v0.1.9 package, prebuilt archives are published for x64-linux,
arm64-linux, and arm64-osx. This port does not distribute newer stable
releases.
Intel macOS (x64-osx) is not a supported platform for new releases; the port
rejects it rather than falling back to a source build. Unsupported Linux
triples without a matching prebuilt asset can install with the from-source
feature:

    vcpkg install 'lance-c[from-source]'

Source builds require a Rust toolchain, CMake, and protoc on the build host.
